<title>BELGIUM: EU TO HOLD WEEKLY SUGAR EXPORT TENDER ON WEDNESDAY.</title>
<headline>EU TO HOLD WEEKLY SUGAR EXPORT TENDER ON WEDNESDAY.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union will on Wednesday hold a regular white sugar export tender, EU member state officials said.</p>
<p>They said that the tender would be the main item on an otherwise low-key agenda for the weekly EU sugar management committee.</p>
<p>&quot;It's August, it's very quiet with most people on holiday,&quot; an official said.</p>
<p>Last week at the first tender of the 1997/98 export season, the EU approved the export of 28,000 tonnes of white sugar at a maximum rebate of 39.437 Ecus per 100 kg.</p>
<p>On Wednesday, the EU will also set fortnightly white and raw sugar export refunds and review duties on imports of molasses.</p>
<p>-Brussels newsroom +322 287 6830</p>
